<section class="content-section">
  <div class="prose-content">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Sourcing Decision</h2>
    <p>Organisations struggle to decide which operations to run in-house and which to outsource. The decision is often driven by habit or vendor pressure, not by a structured analysis of cost, risk, and capability. Without a defensible framework, leadership teams are left justifying choices that may have been made on incomplete information.</p>
    <p>Our approach addresses this gap directly. We assess your current operations against a maturity model, model the total cost of ownership for in-house versus outsourced models, and evaluate managed service providers against your specific requirements. The outcome is a sourcing decision framework, a cost comparison model, a provider evaluation, and a transition plan for the selected model.</p>
    <p>Whether the answer is to keep, outsource, or adopt a hybrid model, you will have the evidence to support it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

