<section class="content-section-alt">
  <p class="eyebrow">How We Work</p>
  <h2 class="section-title">Our Process</h2>
  <div class="process-grid">
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="stat-box">
        <div class="stat-value">01</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Baseline</div>
      </div>
      <p>We document your current operations, costs, headcount, and service levels. This forms the factual foundation for all subsequent analysis.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="stat-box">
        <div class="stat-value">02</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Cost Modelling</div>
      </div>
      <p>We build a three-year total cost of ownership comparison for in-house, outsourced, and hybrid models. This includes direct costs, indirect costs, and transition costs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="stat-box">
        <div class="stat-value">03</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Risk Assessment</div>
      </div>
      <p>We identify the risks of each model — loss of control, vendor lock-in, transition risk, and service-level exposure. Each risk is scored and mapped to mitigation strategies.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="stat-box">
        <div class="stat-value">04</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Provider Evaluation</div>
      </div>
      <p>If outsourcing is viable, we evaluate providers against your requirements using weighted criteria. The evaluation covers technical capability, commercial terms, and cultural fit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="stat-box">
        <div class="stat-value">05</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Transition Plan</div>
      </div>
      <p>We build the transition roadmap with knowledge transfer, phased handover, and service-level governance. The plan is designed to minimise operational disruption.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Example Outcomes</p>
  <h2 class="section-title">What This Looks Like in Practice</h2>
  <div class="prose-content">
    <p>These are illustrative scenarios based on the types of engagements we deliver. They demonstrate the range of outcomes a structured sourcing analysis can produce.</p>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>A regional retailer avoided building a 24/7 SOC when the cost model showed a managed service would deliver equivalent coverage at a fraction of the three-year total cost of ownership.</li>
      <li>A government agency used a hybrid model — keeping incident response in-house while outsourcing monitoring and Tier-1 triage to balance control with cost efficiency.</li>
      <li>A remote-first SaaS company transitioned its infrastructure operations to a managed provider over six months, retaining two engineers for architecture and escalation.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

